    "gates": "Launch and prepare each of four independent processes sequentially. Hold their existing enable acknowledgments until all are ready. Execute complete phases in ABBA/BAAB order, holding each disable acknowledgment until every process finishes. Only then permit output serialization, validation and exit.",
    "runtime": "Reuse byte-identical original before/after release executables; no switch, source change, seed override, replay or build. Every plan is executed once and dropped as in the original benchmark.",
    "statistics": "Each group has two independent processes per label. Primary: ratio of the average process medians. Secondary: ratio of full-label means. Bootstrap whole four-process groups within four predetermined blocks, 10000 resamples, seed 88. Also report instruction changes. Do not treat within-process executions as independent process samples.",
    "acceptance": "Both original/original and candidate/candidate time intervals must fit within +/-1% and include zero. Candidate/original primary and secondary upper bounds must be below +0.5%, with no resolved positive effect. Retain all previous evidence even on a pass.",
    "stopping_rule": "One fixed 32-group, 128-process schedule, no discarded groups or extensions for a preferred result. Smoke checks and other work finish before cooldown and measurement.",
    "limits": [
      "The four processes remain resident while each phase runs; allocation lifetime and cache/predictor history differ from sequential process launch.",
      "Whole phases remain separate in time; this does not interleave individual query executions.",
      "Conditional intervals cover this fixed host and schedule without multiple-comparison correction."
    ]
